      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems a bit misleading. If allocating the root page was the only reason for this VM pool, we could avoid all this dance just by pre-allocating the root page instead of allocating it in pkvm_pgtable_init() (especially since, as it happens, pkvm_pgtable_init() already has a `bool alloc_root` argument for that). The actual major reason, as I see it, is that the pool provides us with the refcounting mechanisms (hyp_get_page/hyp_put_page), not just for the root page but for any pages, even those that are allocated from the memcache, not from the pool itself.\n\n...Ok, just noticed that you mentioned that below: \"This pool is also used as a placeholder for freed pages\". That also might be a bit misleading: as I understand, those freed pages don\u0027t just sit there until the teardown, they are actively allocated (since guest_mmu_zalloc_page() first tries to allocate from the pool and only after that from the memcache).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "f5f577a9c415693f9ed4e5033ab291861997661a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
