      "message": "\u003e But please note that this allocation is still needed and we actually call pkvm_pgtable_init (which BTW is used not only for guest mmu pgtable init) with alloc_root set to true and then it results with calling pgtable_alloc_page-\u003e..-\u003eguest_mmu_zalloc_page which requires some free pages either from memcache or per-VM pool.\n\nWhat I meant is that we could simply set `pkvm_vm-\u003emmu.root_pa` to `pgd_pa` before calling `pkvm_pgtable_init()` (and then of course call it, but with `alloc_root` set to false).\n\nAnyway, I\u0027m not suggesting to do that, since root_pa is not the only reason for this per-VM pool anyway.\n\n\u003e How about rephrasing commit log to: [...]\n\nSGTM.",
